infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Same O(N), 17x apart: array vs linked list
  desc 1M elements, N iterations each — memory layout sets the per-element price
  compares
    - label Array — ~1 ms for 1M
      children
        - label Contiguous allocation
          desc Elements at address, +8, +16 … one flat block
        - label Prefetcher hits ahead
          desc Cache lines loaded before the loop arrives; data sits in L1
        - label ~1 ns per element
          desc Nearly every read is a free L1 hit
    - label Linked list — ~100 ms for 1M
      children
        - label Scattered heap nodes
          desc Each .next points to a random address
        - label Prefetcher defeated
          desc Hardware cannot predict the next pointer
        - label ~100 ns per node
          desc Cold cache line → full RAM round-trip
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
